    <statement><p>Find a formula for a function <m>g(x,y,z)</m> whose level surfaces are
planes parallel to the plane <m>z = 6x+7y-3</m>.</p>
<p><m>g(x,y,z) =</m> <fillin characters="45" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6x+7y-z</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>6\,\overrightarrow{i}+7\,\overrightarrow{j}-\overrightarrow{k}</m> is
<m>6x+7y-z = c</m>, for some constant <m>c</m>.  Thus we could take
<m>g(x,y,z)=6x+7y-z</m>.  Other answers are possible.




</solution>
